<Base title="There is no right way to use a journal" description="Skip a page. Write one word. Start again when you want to."><article class="prose"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / There is no right way to use a journal</nav><p class="eyebrow">Bloom Library · Using your journal</p><h1>There is no right way to use a journal</h1><p class="smallnote">New editorial draft · I Will Bloom · 17 November 2026</p><p>You do not owe your journal a daily entry. It is there when you want somewhere to put a thought, make a mark or pause for a moment.</p><h2>Make it fit the day</h2><p>On a busy day, one word might be enough. On a quieter day, you might want more room. You can begin in the middle, return to an old prompt or leave something unfinished.</p><h2>Privacy is your choice</h2><p>You can share a page if you want to. You can also keep every word to yourself. Writing something down does not create an obligation to explain it.</p><p>The useful rhythm is the one that suits you.</p><p><a href="/bloom-library/">← Back to the Bloom Library</a></p></article></Base>